  "articleBody": "Exterior painting can dramatically refresh your home's look and protect it from the elements, but it's also a project where certain mistakes can lead to a less-than-stellar outcome. If you're planning an exterior painting project in Allen, knowing what to sidestep can save you time, money, and frustration. You want that fresh coat to last for years, not peel or fade prematurely.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\n\n*   **Skipping Proper Surface Preparation:** Many homeowners underestimate the importance of cleaning, scraping, sanding, and priming. Painting over dirt, mildew, or loose paint means your new paint won't adhere properly, leading to early peeling. **How to avoid it:** A professional painter will dedicate significant time to surface prep, including power washing, scraping all loose paint, and applying a quality primer. They'll ensure the surface is clean, dry, and sound before any paint goes on.\n*   **Ignoring Weather Conditions:** Painting during extreme heat, cold, high humidity, or when rain is expected can compromise the paint's drying and curing process, leading to bubbling, cracking, or uneven finishes. **How to avoid it:** Schedule your project during optimal weather windows. A good contractor will monitor forecasts and adjust schedules to ensure ideal conditions for painting, typically avoiding the hottest parts of the Texas summer or unexpected cold fronts.\n*   **Using Low-Quality Paint and Materials:** Opting for cheaper paint might save money upfront, but it often lacks durability, UV resistance, and coverage, meaning you'll be repainting sooner. **How to avoid it:** Invest in high-quality exterior paints designed for the Texas climate. A professional will use premium paints and materials that offer better protection against moisture, UV exposure, and weather-related wear, ensuring a longer-lasting finish.\n*   **Neglecting Lead-Safe Practices in Older Homes:** If your home in Allen was built before 1978, it likely has lead-based paint. Disturbing this paint without proper precautions can create hazardous dust. **How to avoid it:** For homes built before 1978, ensure your contractor is EPA- or state-certified and uses lead-safe renovators and work practices. This includes containment, dust control, and specific cleanup procedures to protect your family and the environment. Discounted Roofing Co. adheres to professional standards for all exterior work.\n*   **Inadequate Protection of Non-Painted Areas:** Getting paint on landscaping, windows, or walkways is a common DIY slip-up that looks messy and can be hard to clean. **How to avoid it:** A professional team will meticulously protect all non-painted surfaces with tarps, drop cloths, and tape. This attention to detail ensures a clean job site and a crisp finish without overspray or drips.\n\nAvoiding these mistakes means your exterior painting project in Allen will not only look great but also provide lasting protection for your home. Remember, professional help is important when tackling complex projects or working on older homes. Discounted Roofing Co. provides clean, professional painting that shields your home and elevates its curb appeal. Contact us for an estimate on your exterior painting project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
